  "explanation": "The documents present conflicting accounts regarding George Frank Butler's education. Document 1 (D1S5, D1S6) states he attended the University of Rochester for his undergraduate degree and Durham University for his medical degree. Document 2 (D2S5, D2S16) claims he attended Rush Medical College for his medical degree. Since the prompt asks for 'educational institution' and allows for distinct valid referents or competing assertions about one referent without silencing them, all three institutions mentioned as places of study are included. Columbia University Medical Center (C3) is excluded as it is described as a place of residency (training), not the primary educational institution where degrees were earned. The American College of Cardiology (C4) and Journal of the American Medical Association (C5) are professional organizations and journals, respectively, not educational institutions attended for degrees."
